vvaharness 1.5.0 — agentic SAST pipeline

Usage: vvaharness <command> [options]

Commands:
  command    what it does                                                       
  setup      Guided readiness check: AI agents, keys, deps, gateway, config     
  doctor     Check credentials + live backend connectivity (read-only)          
  estimate   Print a rough scope/cost preview for a repo (no API spend)         
  gc         Delete old runs: checkpoints and code-graph workspaces (--keep-runs
             / --max-age-days / --dry-run)                                      
  scan       Scan a repo (or --repo-file batch) for vulnerabilities             
  remediate  Walk findings from a prior scan and remediate them                 
  validate   Run the s11 agentic validation agent on applied remediations       
  ev-replay  Re-check exploit-verified findings against a REDEPLOYED target     
  --version  Print the installed version                                        

Stages
  scan: the packaged default skips S10/S11; --remediate enables S10 only and can edit source.
  scan: in-scan S11 needs step_validate.enabled: true, and --stop-after s9 skips both.
  doctor --cache-probe: opt-in live prompt-cache diagnostic. Spends real tokens (~65-70k/model, printed first); never runs during `scan`.
  remediate: --interactive/-i to pick from a menu; --mode fix|report-only; --top N overrides step_remediate.top_n_findings (--top all remediates every one); --verbose/-v.

Config
  ./config.yaml when present, otherwise the packaged default.
  Customise: cp vvaharness/config/profiles/sdk.yaml config.yaml   (see also full.yaml)
  sdk/full profiles enable S10/S11; default/taint disable them. A local overlay can override these flags.
  Standalone remediate and validate remain available when the scan flags are false.

Quick start
  vvaharness setup
  vvaharness estimate --repo /path/to/target
  vvaharness scan --repo /path/to/target --application-id 12345
  vvaharness scan --repo /path/to/target --stop-after s9   # skip S10/S11 on any profile

Run `vvaharness <command> --help` for a command's own options.
